User Guide: AquaStream360 Weather Application
________________________________________
1. Introduction 
This tool supports water resource management, environmental analysis, and weather data processing. It enables the collection, analysis, and visualization of weather  data to support decision-making in any field where understanding weather data is crucial. Applications include:
•	Water resource management
•	Agricultural planning
•	Climate impact assessment
•	Reservoir and dam operations
•	Environmental monitoring

Key Benefits
•	Data Integration: Combine weather data with any external datasets to analyze interactions or influences
•	Time-Series Analysis: Track patterns over days, months, or years
•	Correlation Studies: Identify relationships between weather and other variables e.g. water demand
•	Professional Reporting: Export analyses and visualizations
•	User-Friendly Interface: Accessible, intuitive controls

________________________________________
2. Weather Analysis Module
Purpose
Analyze historical weather data from NASA POWER database for management applications.
Capabilities
1.	Data Acquisition: Fetch historical satellite and ground measurements
2.	Data Processing: Organize into structured tables
3.	Statistical Analysis: Summarize variables comprehensively
4.	Correlation Analysis: Identify relationships between variables
5.	Visualization: Graphs and charts for pattern recognition
________________________________________
3. Demand Analysis Module
Purpose
Analyze water demand data alongside weather patterns to support management decisions.
Capabilities
•	Monitor water usages or reservoir capacity and discharge 
•	Track storage levels and consumption patterns
•	Analyze seasonal variations
Integration
•	Import from Excel, CSV, or databases
•	Align dates with weather data automatically
•	Generate correlation matrices
________________________________________
4. Flexible Analysis Module
Purpose
Analyze any provided attribute (e.g., crop yield, energy consumption, or other metrics) alongside weather patterns to support management decisions.
Capabilities
•	Monitor the selected attribute over time
•	Track patterns, trends, or fluctuations
•	Analyze seasonal or periodic variations
Integration
•	Import data from Excel, CSV, or databases
•	Align dates automatically with weather or other time-series data
•	Generate correlation matrices or statistical summaries
Note: The module does not assume the type of data you provide. You may be prompted to specify the name of the attribute or variable so the system can incorporate it into analyses and generate meaningful comparisons.

